WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.968
Ten days from now

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:04.604
is the one year anniversary

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.173
when Russia brutally, illegally

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.443
and in a completely unprovoked way

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.812
invaded the sovereign nation of Ukraine.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.549
As the secretary just pointed out.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.851
Putin thought he could defeat

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.651
Ukraine, quickly

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.453
fracture of the NATO alliance

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.322
and act with impunity.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.523
He was wrong.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.892
Ukraine remains free.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.660
They remain independent.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.828
Naito in this coalition

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.964
has never been stronger.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.500
And Russia is now a global pariah.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.703
And the world remains inspired

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.738
by Ukrainian bravery and resilience.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.374
In short, Russia has lost.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.310
They've lost strategically,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.946
operationally and tactically,

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.049
and they are paying an enormous price

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.717
on the battlefield.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.853
But until Putin ends his war of choice,

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.555
the international community

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.657
will continue to support Ukraine

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.192
with the equipment and capability

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.927
it needs to defend itself.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.362
Through this group,

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.630
we are collectively supporting

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.397
Ukraine's ability

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.066
to defend its territory,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.301
protect its citizens, and liberate

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.904
their occupied areas in the face

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.306
of a barbaric Russian invasion.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:16.743
Ukrainians remain resilient.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.845
The nation of Ukraine is united

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.847
for one single purpose

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.682
to expel the Russian forces

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.084
from their territory

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.318
and to defend themselves.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.354
For Ukraine,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.356
this is not a war of aggression.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.359
It is a war of defense

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.394
for Russia.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.863
It is a war of aggression.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:38.765
The Russian military has paid

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.766
tremendous costs

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.701
in their war of aggression,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.169
and now they have resorted

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.305
to sending conscripts and prisoners

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.707
to imminent death.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.442
In recent months,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:49.876
the group

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:50.710
gathered here today

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.945
pledged to provide significant

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:54.347
quantities of battlefield capabilities

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.516
tanks, air defense and munitions

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.219
11 countries have pledged tanks.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.954
22 have pledged

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:01.955
infantry fighting vehicles.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.591
16 pledged artillery and munitions,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.259
and nine more

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.027
pledged air defense artillery.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.863
The group is focused

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.930
focused on delivering

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.465
the capabilities committed

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.534
and efficiently, providing the training,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.169
the spare parts, the sustainment

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.037
logistics necessary

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.340
for the full employment of these systems.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.809
Training, maintaining and sustaining

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.045
Ukraine's remains key for Ukraine.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:26.646
To prevail

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.448
throughout this war.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.883
Ukraine has shown

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.951
incredible resourcefulness

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.686
in how they integrate very capabilities

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:34.687
to adapt

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.788
the changing dynamics

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.257
of this battlefield.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.291
Ukrainians have combined

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.027
unbreakable will with innovative tactics

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.195
and empower

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.263
their leaders

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.999
to liberate their own country.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.534
Russia, on contrast,

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:50.370
is waging a very costly war of attrition,

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:53.506
while Ukraine is effectively

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.341
leveraging their asymmetric advantages

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.143
in order to defend itself.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.111
And the most important

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.045
asymmetric advantage

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.146
they have

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.948
is courage, resilience

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.983
and tactical skill.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.553
This war is extremely dynamic,

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.688
and Ukraine today is fighting

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.590
while training and evolving

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.392
future operations.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.593
Ukraine will integrate recent

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.794
commitments of armored vehicles

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.262
infantry fighting vehicles

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.498
and tanks with fires

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.200
to achieve the effect

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.535
of synchronized ground maneuver.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.903
While Russia has waged this war

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.438
for far too long.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.673
They will not outlast

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.141
the Ukrainian people,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.642
nor the group of allies and

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.810
partners that met today.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.579
The purpose for the

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.714
United States and allies

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.183
as said by our political leadership,

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.685
is very simple.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:39.752
It's to uphold the rules

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.888
based international order in order

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.089
that rejects the idea

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.225
that big, strong powerful nations

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.227
can attack other smaller countries,

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.096
that borders shall not change

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.065
just by the use of aggressive

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:53.333
military force.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.301
This is the very underlying

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.037
founding principle of the United Nations.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.840
At the end of World War Two,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.810
Ukraine does not stand alone

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.012
54 countries met today

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.248
to ensure that Ukraine can defend itself

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.849
and the principles

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.884
that guide international conduct.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.520
And those principles will be upheld.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.557
We will remain a unified coalition.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.992
We will continue to uphold the values

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.593
of sovereignty and freedom

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.996
and will continue to support Ukraine.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.998
Thank you and I welcome your questions.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.633
Thank you both, gentlemen.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.001
Yutaka Abe,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.806
Secretary Austin,

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.474
you said earlier

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.309
this is a crucial moment for Ukraine

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.010
and that the

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.611
allies need to get air defenses

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.980
and munitions into Ukraine now.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.515
What are you seeing from Russia

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.751
that makes this moment different?

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.552
And the NATO's secretary general

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.553
has already warned

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.955
that Ukraine is burning

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:49.822
through munitions

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:50.857
faster than a rate

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.925
that the allies can supply it.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.394
Will you at some point

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.697
need to ask Ukraine to do more with less

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.567
And then for Chairman Milley,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.802
did one of the missiles

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.104
fired at the Lake Huron object, Miss.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.441
And if so, what happened to that missile?

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.443
And if so, does that change

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.512
your risk calculus for shooting down

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:14.480
objects over U.S. soil?

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.683
Are you starting to develop alternatives?

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.551
If, if and when

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.952
you detect the next object

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.222
so in terms of where

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.857
we are, thanks to our

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.160
terms of where we are in the fight,

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.461
what we see,

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.295
what we've seen over

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:32.665
the last several months,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.202
is a contested battlefield.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.072
We see a lot of activity in

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.842
in the mood area which is where Russia is

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.211
is focusing most of its effort.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.680
We see Russia

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:51.284
introducing a number of new troops

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:52.719
to the battlefield.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:55.455
Many of those troops are ill trained

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:58.057
and in and ill equipped.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.828
And so their casualty rate

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:04.697
has been really high

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.468
What Ukraine wants to do in the

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:09.602
you know,

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.472
at the first possible moment is to

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:16.576
establish or create

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.245
momentum and in

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.882
and establish

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.283
conditions on the battlefield.

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:26.986
That continue to be in its favor.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.989
And so we expect to see them

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:33.659
conduct an

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.429
offensive sometime in the spring.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.498
And because of that,

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:41.200
we are we all the partners in the

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.036
in the Ukraine Defense Contact Group

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:45.772
have been working hard

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:46.639
to ensure

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:50.109
that they have the armored capability,

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.178
the fires

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.045
the sustainment,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.548
to be able to be effective

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:56.916
in creating the effects

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:57.583
on the battlefield

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.352
that they want to create.

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.686
And so

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.388
we believe that there will be

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.590
a window of opportunity

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.124
for them

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:05.992
to exercise

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.895
our initiative and then change

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:12.832
or continue to to

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.601
create the right conditions

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:16.402
on the battlefield

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.771
or in terms of munitions.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:20.740
This has been a tough fight throughout.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:21.874
And we've been.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.110
Ukraine has been at this for a year.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.012
And so they have used

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:28.080
a lot of artillery ammunition.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:29.749
We're going to do everything

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:30.783
we can working with

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.819
our international partners to ensure that

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:34.821
we give them as much

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:38.691
ammunition as quickly as as possible,

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.860
and that we'll do everything

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:41.227
we can

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.696
to sustain our efforts there as well.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.133
We are working to

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:49.235
with the Ukrainian soldiers

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.904
in various places throughout Europe

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:52.872
to emphasize

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:55.341
