00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.790
for the Ukrainian armed forces.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.025
They they pick this stuff up

00:10:59.025 --> 00:10:59.458
and they do that

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:00.960
and they practice all the good

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.328
tactics, techniques and procedures

00:11:02.328 --> 00:11:03.796
that I just described.

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:04.196
I would say

00:11:04.196 --> 00:11:05.798
it's not without risk, but it's moderate

00:11:05.798 --> 00:11:06.766
and it's been successful so

00:11:06.766 --> 00:11:07.433
far to get through.

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:09.435
Let's go to Felicia

00:11:09.435 --> 00:11:11.537
Schwartz, Financial Times

00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:16.142
Thank you.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.712
First for Secretary Austin,

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:20.312
we've heard

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:21.747
from Western officials

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:24.750
that Russia's Air Force is well intact

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.919
and that the Russians are preparing

00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:27.720
to launch

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:29.288
an air campaign as its land

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:31.090
forces are depleted.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.291
Where is Russia

00:11:32.291 --> 00:11:34.427
amassing aircraft ahead of the offensive?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.328
How soon could this begin?

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:37.329
Has this hastened

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:38.431
the need to provide

00:11:38.431 --> 00:11:39.999
air defense to Ukraine

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:41.100
and has enough assistance

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:41.767
been provided

00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:42.768
so that Ukraine is

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:44.904
ready to defend against it?

00:11:44.904 --> 00:11:47.339
And then for Chairman Milley,

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:48.841
Does Russia have the right equipment

00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:49.241
to pose

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:50.509
a threat to the Ukrainians

00:11:50.509 --> 00:11:52.378
and break through in the Donbass?

00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:53.479
And separately,

00:11:53.479 --> 00:11:54.980
but relatedly, is Ukraine

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.248
going to get enough equipment

00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:57.450
and enough time

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:58.551
and have a big enough force

00:11:58.551 --> 00:11:59.685
on the ground to be able to have

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:01.020
a serious counteroffensive?

00:12:02.822 --> 00:12:04.423
Thanks, Felicia.

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:06.792
In terms of whether or not Russia is

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.795
massing its aircraft

00:12:09.795 --> 00:12:12.932
for some massive aerial attack,

00:12:13.466 --> 00:12:14.900
we don't currently see that.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.902
We do know that Russia has

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.406
a substantial number of aircraft

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:21.440
in its inventory

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.642
and a lot of capability left.

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:23.976
That's why

00:12:23.976 --> 00:12:25.711
we've emphasized that

00:12:25.711 --> 00:12:27.780
we need to do everything that we can

00:12:28.414 --> 00:12:30.216
to get Ukraine as much air

00:12:30.216 --> 00:12:33.185
defense capability as we possibly can.

00:12:33.185 --> 00:12:34.687
And recently,

00:12:34.687 --> 00:12:35.287
you've seen us

00:12:35.287 --> 00:12:37.623
step up and offer patriots.

00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:40.159
You've seen other countries come forward

00:12:40.493 --> 00:12:43.429
with some tea and in Irish tea,

00:12:44.096 --> 00:12:45.898
but it's not enough.

00:12:45.898 --> 00:12:48.000
And we're going to keep pushing until we

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.635
we get more

00:12:49.635 --> 00:12:51.637
because that threat is out there.

00:12:52.037 --> 00:12:53.105
But again,

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:55.207
we many countries

00:12:55.207 --> 00:12:57.643
have stepped up to the plate thus far.

00:12:57.643 --> 00:12:58.711
Our effort

00:12:58.711 --> 00:13:00.980
currently is to get these capabilities

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.281
into country

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:04.550
as quickly as we can

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.752
and then integrate those capabilities

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:07.787
So we have truly

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:09.355
have an integrated air

00:13:09.355 --> 00:13:11.657
and missile defense capability.

00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:12.725
And I would add that

00:13:12.725 --> 00:13:15.027
Ukraine has done a credible job of

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:17.129
of intercepting a lot of the

00:13:18.464 --> 00:13:19.532
rockets and missiles that

00:13:19.532 --> 00:13:21.767
have been launched by by Russia

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:23.702
in those recent attacks.

00:13:23.702 --> 00:13:24.670
But again,

00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:25.938
we want to make sure

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:26.839
that they have the ability

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:28.474
to protect themselves

00:13:28.474 --> 00:13:30.075
going forward in the event

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:30.910
that Russia tries

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.311
to introduce

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:34.713
its Air Force into this fight.

00:13:34.713 --> 00:13:35.281
They haven't done

00:13:35.281 --> 00:13:36.849
so thus far because

00:13:36.849 --> 00:13:37.616
Ukraine's

00:13:37.616 --> 00:13:38.250
air defenses

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.285
have been pretty strong,

00:13:39.285 --> 00:13:41.086
effective, as you know.

00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:43.122
So foolish on on

00:13:43.122 --> 00:13:43.956
whether or not the Russians

00:13:43.956 --> 00:13:45.391
have the capability and equipment, etc.

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:47.760
to continue the attack in the Donbas.

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.562
They are attacking in the Donbas

00:13:49.562 --> 00:13:50.496
right now.

00:13:50.763 --> 00:13:51.797
Their progress is slow.

00:13:51.797 --> 00:13:52.665
It's a war of attrition.

00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:54.433
They take heavy casualties.

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:56.936
Their leadership and morale is not great.

00:13:56.936 --> 00:13:58.571
And they're struggling mightily.

00:13:58.571 --> 00:14:00.773
However, they do have numbers.

00:14:01.373 --> 00:14:03.209
And as you know,

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:03.776
President Putin

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:04.643
did a call up of

00:14:04.643 --> 00:14:06.178
several hundred thousand.

00:14:06.178 --> 00:14:07.112
And those folks

00:14:07.112 --> 00:14:08.747
have been arriving on the battlefield.

00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:11.083
So they do have numbers.

00:14:11.083 --> 00:14:12.017
And whether or not

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:12.818
they're successful

00:14:12.818 --> 00:14:15.120
in suppressing the fight

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.155
That remains to be seen.

00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:18.290
But that fight has been going on,

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.124
and it's a slow,

00:14:19.124 --> 00:14:20.993
grinding battle of attrition in that

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:22.394
in that general area.

00:14:22.394 --> 00:14:23.128
For the Ukrainians,

00:14:23.128 --> 00:14:24.697
I don't want to project forward

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:26.565
what the Ukrainians may or may not do.

00:14:26.565 --> 00:14:27.032
As you know

00:14:27.032 --> 00:14:29.401
from this particular conference here,

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:30.603
we are

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:31.804
placing that up

00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:32.738
with a significant amount

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:34.506
of capabilities

00:14:34.506 --> 00:14:36.809
with ground maneuver, artillery, etc..

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:38.244
What they do with that,

00:14:38.244 --> 00:14:39.411
that'll be up to the Ukrainians

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:41.380
in the coming weeks and months.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.248
We have time for one more.

00:14:42.248 --> 00:14:43.182
Let's go to Marcus Price.

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:44.016
Early television

00:14:48.621 --> 00:14:49.655
Thank you very much.

00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:52.758
One question to Secretary Austan

00:14:52.758 --> 00:14:54.727
about the stance of the U.S.

00:14:54.727 --> 00:14:57.563
when it comes to delivery of fighter jets

00:14:57.563 --> 00:14:59.398
and the president Biden said

00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:01.500
no to the delivery of F-16.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.202
Also early in the conflict

00:15:03.202 --> 00:15:05.371
when Poland offered to deliver MiG

00:15:05.638 --> 00:15:08.274
29 via Rammstein to Ukraine.

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:10.342
I think the U.S. stopped it.

00:15:10.342 --> 00:15:12.611
Has this position evolved?

00:15:13.445 --> 00:15:15.814
Do you encourage countries to do

00:15:15.814 --> 00:15:17.816
so if they want to,

00:15:17.816 --> 00:15:19.485
or do we assess the risk is too high?

00:15:19.485 --> 00:15:20.452
So what is the U.S.

00:15:20.452 --> 00:15:21.787
position on other countries

00:15:21.787 --> 00:15:23.155
delivering fighter jets

00:15:23.155 --> 00:15:26.158
and to Chairman Milley,

00:15:26.158 --> 00:15:28.227
the Russian offensive we are seeing?

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:30.262
What do you see so far?

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:31.597
Is this very serious?

00:15:31.597 --> 00:15:32.431
Is it different

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:34.500
than what we saw in the past?

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.669
And do you have any intelligence

00:15:36.669 --> 00:15:37.503
whether we see

00:15:37.503 --> 00:15:38.904
and we are going to see

00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:41.206
another attempt of the Russian forces

00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:42.841
to capture Kiev? Thank you.

00:15:44.877 --> 00:15:47.913
Thanks, Marcus, for the record.

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.783
With respect to any kind of aircraft

00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:53.052
being provided by Poland,

00:15:53.052 --> 00:15:54.720
the United States never stopped

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.889
Poland from providing anything.

00:15:58.557 --> 00:16:01.593
A decision to provide something is

00:16:02.795 --> 00:16:03.529
is.

00:16:04.229 --> 00:16:05.464
That's the

00:16:05.931 --> 00:16:07.299
you know, the

00:16:07.633 --> 00:16:08.567
decision made

00:16:08.567 --> 00:16:09.635
that there will be a decision

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.170
made by the leadership of that country.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:11.904
That's certainly not

00:16:11.904 --> 00:16:14.273
something that we can or will dictate

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.642
in terms of

00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:17.910
whether or not

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.878
we're going to provide F-16s.

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:21.246
As I said earlier,

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:23.182
I don't have any announcements to make

00:16:23.182 --> 00:16:25.317
and I don't have anything to add to

00:16:25.985 --> 00:16:27.820
what our president said earlier.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:31.156
So I'll just leave it at that.

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:33.625
And Marcus, on the issue of the

00:16:34.326 --> 00:16:35.227
Russian offensive, this

00:16:35.227 --> 00:16:36.261
this offensive that you see

00:16:36.261 --> 00:16:37.596
ongoing right now

00:16:37.596 --> 00:16:40.132
in the generally in the Bachmann area,

00:16:40.833 --> 00:16:42.001
you know, from from Kharkiv,

00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:44.003
all the way down to Curtis on

00:16:44.003 --> 00:16:46.338
the front line is quite stable,

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:47.406
even though very violent

00:16:47.406 --> 00:16:48.540
and a lot of fighting.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:49.742
It's relatively stable.

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:52.945
Most of the dynamic movement back

00:16:52.945 --> 00:16:53.412
and forth

00:16:53.412 --> 00:16:54.179
is in generally

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:56.115
in the vicinity of buck mode.

00:16:56.115 --> 00:16:58.017
The Ukrainians are holding

00:16:58.017 --> 00:16:58.951
they're fighting the defense,

00:16:58.951 --> 00:16:59.685
the Russians

00:16:59.685 --> 00:17:01.020
primarily involved in the group

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.788
or attacking parties.

00:17:02.788 --> 00:17:03.822
What I would describe it

00:17:03.822 --> 00:17:04.823
as is a

00:17:04.823 --> 00:17:07.626
really a very significant grinding

00:17:07.626 --> 00:17:08.861
battle of attrition

00:17:08.861 --> 00:17:10.396
with very high casualties,

00:17:10.396 --> 00:17:11.663
especially on the Russian side.

00:17:12.631 --> 00:17:14.233
There's no fancy

00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:15.734
arts of maneuver going on here.

00:17:15.734 --> 00:17:17.803
This is frontal attacks, wave attacks,

00:17:17.803 --> 00:17:19.471
lots of artillery

00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:21.774
with extremely high levels of casualties.

00:17:22.207 --> 00:17:23.842
In that particular area.

00:17:23.842 --> 00:17:25.844
And how long that will last

00:17:25.844 --> 00:17:27.379
is difficult to say, actually.

00:17:27.379 --> 00:17:29.214
It's been going on for weeks,

00:17:29.214 --> 00:17:31.750
and I think it'll continue to go on

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.552
until the until the either

00:17:33.552 --> 00:17:35.120
the Russians culminate.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.722
I don't think the Ukrainians will

00:17:36.722 --> 00:17:37.689
just collapse or fall.

00:17:37.689 --> 00:17:38.557
I think they're going to continue

00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:38.957
to fight.

00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:41.326
So that that's a battle worth the

00:17:41.727 --> 00:17:43.128
but with that, we're paying attention

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:44.029
to very, very closely

00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:45.064
and making sure that the Ukrainians

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:46.965
have the capability to continue to defend

00:17:46.965 --> 00:17:48.300
as far as Kyiv.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:48.934
I'm not going to

00:17:48.934 --> 00:17:50.702
what intelligence we have or don't have.

00:17:50.702 --> 00:17:52.738
I would just say that right now

00:17:53.138 --> 00:17:54.440
there's always a potential threat.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:56.175
There's clearly air threats,

00:17:56.175 --> 00:17:57.476
missile attack threats.

00:17:57.476 --> 00:17:59.111
Kyiv is the capital.

00:17:59.111 --> 00:18:00.112
And that was a significant

00:18:00.112 --> 00:18:01.046
objective early in the war.

00:18:01.046 --> 00:18:02.748
So I would never discount

00:18:02.748 --> 00:18:05.150
Russian capabilities to attack you.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.085
But right now, we're not seeing

00:18:06.085 --> 00:18:07.553
any significant indicators and warnings.

